# One git patch filename per line, applied in order to .runtime/behavior (and
# .runtime/behavior-g1 and .runtime/behavior-dex). Ported from RoboEnv:
# 0001 OmniGibson's dataset-recording and LeRobot wrappers become optional imports and extras;
# 0002 OMNIGIBSON_RENDER_GPU selects Isaac's Vulkan renderer apart from the CUDA physics device.
# And rosbridge's own:
# 0003 BehaviorTask.get_goal_option_satisfaction (the evaluator's q_score) evaluates each distinct
#      grounded goal literal once; a quantified goal repeats them across many options.
# 0004 Macro particle systems update the physics handles once per batch of particles added or
#      removed, not per particle; once per batch of visual particles removed too: removing any prim
#      drops the articulation views' handles.
# 0005 A slicer cuts a sliceable or diceable object when it is active, touches it and reaches it
#      with its blade (its slicer meta link's box, 5 mm larger), not with any part while any slicer
#      is active; the slicer that cut is inactive until 2 s after it last touched whole or cut
#      food, not whole food only.
# 0006 A particle remover by projection (the vacuum) takes a visual particle within 1 cm of its
#      volume, which OmniGibson sets below its meta link: under the floor a vacuum stands on.
0001-optional-workflows.patch
0002-gpu-selection.patch
0003-goal-option-literals.patch
0004-particle-handle-updates.patch
0005-slicer-blade.patch
0006-projection-remover-margin.patch
